If you like Coffee and happen to subscribe to James Hoffmann's channel, you'll know he made a Coffee and Donut drink. 
Donut Ice Cream or even donut infused milk, isn't new though, Dana Cree made a Donut Ice cream in her book "Hello, my name is Ice Cream". 

Today's tub is a combination of a donut ice cream and a couple of different coffee ice creams. 

The batching up is easy as you'll see in the video, I stopped my donut ice cream churn a few minutes early so as to make sure it would fill the entire void left in the tub. So with all that in mind......let's get to it!

Coffee Ice Cream Ingredients:
400ml Milk
200ml Double (Heavy) cream
130g Sugar
25g Skimmed Milk Powder
2-3 Tsp Instant coffee OR 50g Coffee bean ground coursew

Donut Ice Cream:
400ml Milk
200ml Double (Heavy) cream
120 Sugar
25g Skimmed Milk Powder
6 Original Glazed Donuts (4 will do but at a push)


You can do a Duo Tub with whatever flavours you want, tag us on social media with your creations as we'd love to see them. 

